The upstream copyright and license notices are preserved. Contributions by
other upstream contributors are recorded in the git history.

Modifications
-------------
Modifications by Blue Pine Solutions, 2026-09-28 through 2026-10-04 (the
dates of the first and most recent downstream commits at the time of
writing; this notice is updated as further modifications are made).

Downstream changes in this repository to date, in two groups.

Distribution, licensing and self-hosting changes (2026-09-28 to 2026-09-29):

- Manual (self-hosted) domain setup works without Cloudflare credentials.
- MX setup for manually managed domains no longer attempts a Cloudflare
  lookup.
- The inbound SMTP listener rejects recipients that do not exist on this
  installation instead of accepting them.
- Forwarding on the self-hosted (Node) runtime now adds the
  X-Mailflare-Forwarded loop-protection header, as the other runtimes do.
- Custom branding, multiple accounts, shared mailboxes and account
  forwarding are governed by a Blue Pine feature policy instead of
  upstream's commercial license tiers.
- Upstream's commercial licensing integration (Paymug license activation
  and the related pricing and upgrade screens) has been removed.
- The product is identified as Blue Pine Solutions Mail, with an About
  page and a source link in the application, and user-facing text names
  Blue Pine Solutions Mail or the administrator's configured app name.
  Releases 0.1.0 and 0.1.1 were published under the earlier name Blue
  Pine Mail; the repository and release tag names keep that form.
- Upstream's in-app updater, which replaced an installation with the
  latest upstream code, has been removed. The application now only checks
  for approved Blue Pine Solutions Mail releases and never installs them
  itself.
- The documentation describes the Blue Pine Solutions Mail distribution;
  upstream sponsorship, pricing and promotional material has been removed.
- Upstream Mailflare changes were merged into this distribution on
  2026-09-29, and dependencies were updated. Downstream guard tests and
  the UPSTREAM.md integration contract record where this distribution
  follows or diverges from upstream.

Mail protocol and storage changes (2026-09-29 to 2026-10-04), all authored
by Blue Pine Solutions and not present in upstream Mailflare:

- Mail app passwords: per-mailbox credentials, scoped to IMAP and/or SMTP
  submission and shown once at creation, with a settings screen and API to
  manage them. Only a hash is stored. Changing the web password, or
  removing access to a shared mailbox, revokes the affected credentials.
- Canonical message storage: a canonical stored representation of each
  message, with background maintenance, used by the IMAP server and the
  original-message download.
- An IMAP server (Node/Docker runtime only, off unless configured, over
  implicit TLS): mailbox listing and selection, persistent UID and flag
  state, FETCH, SEARCH, read-write flags, IDLE, UIDPLUS, MOVE, COPY, draft
  APPEND, recoverable deletion and permanent expunge, mailbox
  create/rename/delete and stored subscriptions, with connection and
  resource limits. Related folder-management changes were made to the web
  application's mailbox folder handling.
- Authenticated SMTP submission (Node/Docker runtime only, off unless
  configured, over implicit TLS): AUTH PLAIN/LOGIN with SMTP-scoped mail
  app passwords, sender authorization against the authenticated mailbox,
  reconstruction of submitted MIME messages for sending, and rate,
  concurrency and size limits.
- Send-path changes: typed delivery results that distinguish rejection,
  temporary failure and unknown outcome, error text that omits bound
  parameters, Reply-To support, and a server-owned copy of each submitted
  message in the Sent folder, so clients should not store their own.
- Inbound SMTP hardening: a concurrent-connection limit and bounded
  buffering of oversized DATA, which disconnects peers that keep sending
  well past the size limit.
- Five additive database migrations (bp0001 to bp0005, with their schema
  in src/db/schema/bluepine.ts) that add the app-password, IMAP mailbox
  state and IMAP subscription tables and triggers. They run after, and
  leave unchanged, upstream's migrations.
- The Docker image and Node server start and configure the IMAP and
  submission listeners (additional exposed ports 465 and 993), and the
  embedded SQLite adapter's batch transactions were made atomic.
- Added documentation, tests, verification scripts and certification
  reports for the above, including checks with a real mail client.

The git history of https://github.com/blue-pine-solutions/blue-pine-mail
identifies each change individually, and preserves upstream's history.

